# App Tone v1 — `(app)` Visual Direction

Before implementing or restyling `(app)` UI, read:

1. [docs/visual-direction.md](../../docs/visual-direction.md) — **App Tone v1** (short)
2. [docs/design-system.md](../../docs/design-system.md) — tokens & patterns
3. [docs/typography.md](../../docs/typography.md) — typo tokens & WebView scale

## Must follow

- **Neutral chrome:** Tab/header **selection** uses `text-primary` / `text-secondary` + `font-semibold` + outline→filled icons — **not** `--color-action-primary`.
- **Action blue only for:** primary CTA buttons, text links, `:focus-visible` ring.
- **Borders:** `--color-border-subtle` for chrome dividers; `--color-border` for cards/inputs.
- **Typography:** `typo-*` classes or `<Typography role="…">` — no Tailwind `text-sm` / `text-lg` in `(app)`.
- **Motion:** subtle (≈150–360ms), tap scale / crossfade; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Reference implementation:** `PrimaryNavBottom`, `NavTabItem`, `nav-icons.tsx`.

## Scope

- Apply to `(app)` routes and their components only.
- Do not extend App Tone v1 to `admin`, `(customer)`, or `login` unless explicitly asked.
